WEBVTT

00:00:06.094 --> 00:00:08.430
(ANNOUNCEMENT IN ITALIAN OVER PA)

00:00:08.513 --> 00:00:10.348
And you have your lunch for the train?

00:00:10.432 --> 00:00:12.726
-Sì.
-Sweater? If it gets cold?

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:15.228
For the millionth time, sì.

00:00:15.312 --> 00:00:17.355
I love you, too, Papà.

00:00:19.399 --> 00:00:21.985
Santa mozzarella, we did it.

00:00:22.068 --> 00:00:24.404
Well, Giulia,
can't wait to race next summer.

00:00:24.487 --> 00:00:26.573
Or we could just have fun.

00:00:28.408 --> 00:00:29.701
Ciao, Giulia.

00:00:32.496 --> 00:00:34.331
(BIDS GOODBYE IN ITALIAN)

00:00:39.085 --> 00:00:40.086
(SIGHS)

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.797
Well, let's go fix up our Vespa.

00:00:42.881 --> 00:00:44.716
Yeah, about that. Uh...

00:00:44.799 --> 00:00:47.302
It's a crazy thing. I might have sold it.

00:00:50.805 --> 00:00:51.806
DANIELA: Luca?

00:00:52.057 --> 00:00:54.643
Mom? What are you all doing here?

00:00:56.102 --> 00:01:00.190
If you promise to write to us
every single day

00:01:00.273 --> 00:01:03.485
and be as safe as possible,
and I mean safer than safe,

00:01:04.236 --> 00:01:07.113
(SIGHS) you can go to school.

00:01:07.572 --> 00:01:08.824
(GASPS) I can?

00:01:08.907 --> 00:01:10.492
It's all arranged, actually.

00:01:10.575 --> 00:01:12.577
You'd stay with Giulia and her mom.

00:01:12.661 --> 00:01:14.538
Your friend talked them into it.

00:01:14.621 --> 00:01:15.914
It wasn't easy.

00:01:18.208 --> 00:01:19.751
Luca, do you promise?

00:01:19.835 --> 00:01:21.545
Yes! Yes, I promise!

00:01:22.295 --> 00:01:23.505
Thank you.

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:28.677
Oh. Just remember,
we are always here for you.

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:29.761
Okay?

00:01:30.595 --> 00:01:32.722
Hey. Look me in the eye.

00:01:33.598 --> 00:01:35.475
You know I love you, right?

00:01:35.559 --> 00:01:37.561
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY) I know.

00:01:41.648 --> 00:01:42.649
(SIGHS)

00:01:43.066 --> 00:01:45.110
Come on, Alberto. The train's gonna leave.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:48.822
Where's your stuff?

00:01:49.614 --> 00:01:51.700
Yeah, well, you see...

00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:53.285
You are coming, right?

00:01:53.702 --> 00:01:57.998
Um, I would, but Massimo asked
if I wanted to stick around.

00:01:58.081 --> 00:02:00.917
Move in maybe. And I just thought, uh...

00:02:02.169 --> 00:02:04.796
I think he needs me.
(CHUCKLES) You know?

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.842
I can't do it without you.

00:02:08.925 --> 00:02:10.427
ALBERTO: But you're never without me.

00:02:13.054 --> 00:02:14.973
The next time that you jump off a cliff

00:02:15.056 --> 00:02:17.726
or tell Bruno to quit bothering you,

00:02:18.101 --> 00:02:19.352
that's me.

00:02:20.145 --> 00:02:23.356
But how am I gonna know you're okay?

00:02:31.281 --> 00:02:33.116
You got me off the island, Luca.

00:02:34.201 --> 00:02:35.368
(SNIFFLES)

00:02:35.452 --> 00:02:36.495
I'm okay.

00:02:39.247 --> 00:02:41.208
-(ENGINE HISSES)
-(HORN TOOTS)

00:02:41.625 --> 00:02:43.627
(GREETING IN ITALIAN)

00:02:45.545 --> 00:02:48.798
(CHUCKLES) Seriously,
what does that mean?

00:02:48.965 --> 00:02:51.510
No idea. Go find out for me, will ya?

00:02:52.761 --> 00:02:54.471
(TRAIN CHUGGING)

00:03:01.686 --> 00:03:03.647
Go, Luca!

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.315
Go!

00:03:05.398 --> 00:03:08.360
Yeah! Whoo-hoo!

00:03:08.443 --> 00:03:10.445
(SENTIMENTAL ORCHESTRAL MUSIC PLAYING)

00:03:15.075 --> 00:03:16.159
(SNIFFLES)

00:03:29.714 --> 00:03:31.716
(SENTIMENTAL ORCHESTRAL MUSIC CONTINUES)

00:03:47.524 --> 00:03:49.526
(LIGHT ITALIAN POP MUSIC PLAYING)

